      "title": "Israeli leader Netanyahu accused of using ‘ugly’ smear tactics to cling to power",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/29/israeli-leader-netanyahu-accused-of-using-ugly-smear-tactics-to-cling-to-power",
      "description": "<p>Prime minister claims Arab Israeli parties used foreign backing to steal elections, in which his coalition lost its majority</p><p>• <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/29/israel-election-results-live-updates-poll-netanyahu-eisenkot-bloc-coalition-latest-news\">Israel election – latest updates</a></p><p>Benjamin Netanyahu has been accused of using smear tactics to cling to power, after he claimed that Arab Israeli parties had used foreign backing to “steal” Tuesday’s election, in which the prime minister’s coalition lost its parliamentary majority.</p><p>Netanyahu and his allies called on the internal security service, Shin Bet, to investigate alleged vote buying and other irregularities in Palestinian communities in Israel, supposedly funded by foreign money.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/29/israeli-leader-netanyahu-accused-of-using-ugly-smear-tactics-to-cling-to-power\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-29T17:26:06"
    },
    {
      "title": "Israel election results live: Qatar says accusations of election interference in Israel ‘ridiculous and dangerous’",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/29/israel-election-results-live-updates-poll-netanyahu-eisenkot-bloc-coalition-latest-news",
      "description": "<p>Netanyahu’s claim of interference in election also dismissed by Israeli police and opposition parties</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/28/israel-elections-choice-netanyahu-remaining-power-or-palestinian-backed-coalition\">Israel’s choice: Netanyahu remaining in power or a Palestinian-backed coalition</a></p></li></ul><p><strong>Gadi Eisenkot,</strong> leader of the Yashar party and Benjamin Netanyahu’s main rival, has warned political opponents against exploiting allegations of foreign interference in Israel’s election to delay the swearing-in of the next Knesset.</p><p>In remarks posted on X, Eisenkot said:</p><p>Israel must safeguard the integrity of the elections against any attempt at interference, spin and manipulation, and examine every complaint thoroughly. On the other hand, <strong>political actors must not be allowed to exploit the situation and affect the swearing-in date of the 26th Knesset.”</strong></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/29/israel-election-results-live-updates-poll-netanyahu-eisenkot-bloc-coalition-latest-news\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-29T17:21:28"
    },
