    {
      "title": "Netanyahu alleges election fraud, rules out cooperation with Arab parties",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/netanyahu-alleges-election-fraud-rules-out-cooperation-with-arab-parties-126102900821_1.html",
      "description": "Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu on Thursday intensified allegations of election fraud by Arab-led parties, describing suspected foreign interference as an \"earthquake\" and demanding an immediate investigation by the police and the country's top internal security agency.\nIn a social media post, Netanyahu cited Central Elections Committee (CEC) chief Justice Noam Sohlberg's decision to ask Shin Bet chief David Zini to investigate suspicions of foreign funding and improper influence in Tuesday's election.\n\"The Ra'amgate affair is an earthquake. They stole the elections in Israel!\" Netanyahu wrote, targeting the Arab-led Ra'am (the United Arab List) and the Joint List alliance.\nHe alleged that foreign entities had interfered in Tuesday's parliamentary elections and bribed voters in favour of Arab-led parties.\nThe allegations come amid an inconclusive election in which neither Netanyahu's bloc nor the opposition camp led by former military chief Gadi Eisenkot has secured a ...",
